`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The peer context reveals a real-world SWAP hazard: one agent deleted all 112 symbols, and another restored them. This shows why `release_symbol` passing `newSource` is architecturally critical — the server can compute a semantic diff and alert peers immediately when a change is destructive rather than additive, enabling faster detection than polling `get_peer_context` manually.
